# locals: (row:)
#
# What the typed columns say about one accessioned row. Rendered by the
# list and by the record page both — the sentence about why `status` is
# here belongs in one place, and so does the shape.
#
# `AccessionFacts` plus where DDBJ has got to with the row. The facts are
# the same ones a reviewer is shown; the status is the difference, and it
# is the difference on purpose — this is the submitter's own screen, and
# a retracted entry not saying so there would be the screen keeping a
# secret from the person it belongs to.
facts = AccessionFacts.for(row)

{
  accession: facts.accession,
  db:        facts.db,
  name:      facts.name,
  details:   facts.details,
  status:    row.status
}
